# Problem Description


An online voting system is a computer program that helps people vote online. It replaces the way of voting with paper. This new way is faster, safer and easier to use.

The system uses a programming language called Python. It helps check who is voting. It makes sure each person can only vote once. It does this by giving each person an ID. The system also adds up the votes away.

The online voting system uses some programming ideas. It uses a list to keep track of votes. It uses loops to keep working all the time. It uses rules to check if the information entered is correct.

This way of voting is better, than the way. It makes mistakes. It costs money to run. It is also more open and honest. This makes it a great tool for groups to make decisions. It is also good for schools to show how to solve problems.

The online voting system is helpful. It makes voting easy and fast. It is a way for people to choose their leaders or make decisions.



# Why it matters?


Digitalizing voting is a step in modernizing how we make decisions in organizations and democracies.

By using an Online Voting System of manual counting we get rid of mistakes and logistical issues that often cause arguments and delays.

In programming building such a system is an exercise in keeping data safe and secure.

We can make sure votes are transparent and secure by giving each voter an ID and counting votes, in real-time.

This way we prevent people from voting

Online voting also makes it easier for people to participate from anywhere which leads to engagement.

As a result the final outcome accurately shows what the community really wants.

Online Voting Systems help ensure that everyones voice is heard.



# My approach to solving it


The approach focuses on Modular Logic and Data Integrity to make sure the voting process is reliable.

It uses a Sentinel-controlled Loop so the program stays active for users and has a clear way to exit.

The core solution uses a Dictionary to add up votes and a Set to keep track of unique Voter IDs.

This helps prevent someone from voting by simply checking if they are already in the Set.

The system also checks user input carefully using try-except blocks.

This way it can handle mistakes like when someone enters something that's not a number.

This approach puts Security first from the start.

It takes the users input. Makes it into election data that can be checked and verified.

The focus is, on Modular Logic, Data Integrity and Security.

The Dictionary and Set are used to make sure votes are counted correctly and that each voter can only vote once.



# Key decisions I made


The main goal was to make sure data is correct by using a list for tracking voters. This list allows us to quickly check if someone is already in it which prevents people from voting

We used a kind of list to keep track of how many votes each candidate got. This makes it easy to update the results as people vote.

* We also added a way to handle mistakes when people enter something that's not a number.

* If someone enters something that's not a number the program will not crash.

* Instead it will let the user know that they made a mistake and ask them to try

The program runs in a loop. Keeps asking the user, for input until they decide to stop.

This makes it easy for people to use the program and vote.

The loop is controlled so it will not do anything

It will keep running until the user chooses to stop it.



